Starting from the stated model for Efficiency and Coefficient of Performance, write the governing mathematical relation and identify the constraint under which it applies.
\[
\eta=\frac{W_{\mathrm{out}}}{Q_H}
=\frac{Q_H-Q_C}{Q_H}
=1-\frac{Q_C}{Q_H}.
\tag*{[1]}
\]
Notation: \(Q_H\) denotes positive hot-reservoir heat magnitude; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(Q_C\) denotes positive cold-reservoir heat magnitude; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(W_{\mathrm{out}}\) denotes positive engine work output; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(W_{\mathrm{in}}\) denotes positive work input to a refrigerator or heat pump; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(\eta\) denotes heat-engine efficiency; dimensionless; \(\mathrm{COP}_R\) denotes refrigerator coefficient of performance; dimensionless; \(\mathrm{COP}_{\mathrm{HP}}\) denotes heat-pump coefficient of performance; dimensionless; \(\dot Q_H,\dot Q_C\) denotes positive hot-side and cold-side heat-transfer rates; unit \(\mathrm{W, W}\); \(P_{\mathrm{out}},P_{\mathrm{in}}\) denotes positive output and input powers; unit \(\mathrm{W, W}\).

